# Surface Pro 9: the accelerometer of the SAM sensor hub (HID over the Surface Aggregator).
#
# The hub sends an accelerometer report only when the reading moved by more than its change
# sensitivity (0.05 g by default), and the SAM HID transport has no way to ask for an input
# report. A buffer enabled while the device rests therefore stays empty, and a read of
# in_accel_*_raw waits 5 s and returns 0. iio-sensor-proxy takes the empty buffer for a broken
# one and falls back to those reads.
#
# Sensitivity 0 makes the hub report at its interval (8 Hz) for as long as something has the
# sensor on (an enabled buffer, a read in progress); nothing is sent while it is off. The kernel
# writes the value again after a system resume.
#
# Sorted before 80-iio-sensor-proxy.rules: the service that rule starts finds the value set.

ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="iio", KERNEL=="iio:device*", SUBSYSTEMS=="surface_aggregator", ATTR{name}=="accel_3d", ATTR{in_accel_hysteresis}="0"
